----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(2) WHY a=1, a=6 survive: the 7-LOCAL (residue-only) selection rule
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   At cell center xi=0: runner v sits at 7-phase (v*a mod 7)/7.  It is at an INTEGER
   (==> central danger) iff v*a ≡ 0 (mod 7).  Tabulate centered-dangerous runners per a:
   a=0: centered-dangerous [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 98]; widest-band runner v=1, needs |xi|>1/2=0.5000 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=1: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=2: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=3: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=4: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=5: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   a=6: centered-dangerous [7, 98]; widest-band runner v=7, needs |xi|>1/14=0.0714 (cell |xi|<1/2)
   ==> mult-of-7 runners {7,98} are centered-dangerous in EVERY cell (residue 0 always).
       Runner 7 forces |xi|>1/14: kills only a 1/7-fraction at each cell center (NOT whole cell).
       So central danger ALONE never empties a cell.  Survival is decided by the NON-central
       (archimedean) bands of the other runners packing the rest of the cell -- next.

