----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(6) LOWER-BOUND CONSEQUENCE: L > 0 reduces to 'some cell has a surviving gap'
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Since L = sum_a m_a and each m_a >= 0, L>0 iff at least one cell has a free gap.
   In a cell, the 13 danger bands have TOTAL length sum_v (#bands_v)*2/(14v).  If this
   total < cell width 1/7, a gap MUST survive (pigeonhole).  Quantify the deficit:
   a=0: total danger-band length (with multiplicity, capped to cell) = 0.450903, cell width = 0.142857  -> bands MAY cover (overlap needed)
   a=1: total danger-band length (with multiplicity, capped to cell) = 0.203451, cell width = 0.142857  -> bands MAY cover (overlap needed)
   a=2: total danger-band length (with multiplicity, capped to cell) = 0.246813, cell width = 0.142857  -> bands MAY cover (overlap needed)
   ==> pigeonhole alone is NOT enough (bands overlap, total ~ cell width); the surviving
       gap in a=1,6 comes from OVERLAP of bands elsewhere freeing room. A rigorous inf>0
       still needs an overlap/structure argument -- but the support is now pinned to 2 cells.

DONE.
